1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:07,590
I am going to tell you a funny incident
from my childhood with my mother. I was

2
00:00:07,630 --> 00:00:14,783
six. We lived in a rural area. We had
two dairy cows. My mother got up early

3
00:00:14,823 --> 00:00:16,989
every day to milk them.

4
00:00:17,650 --> 00:00:23,454
I loved watching my mother milk the cows
and drinking the fresh milk.

5
00:00:24,150 --> 00:00:29,233
One morning my mother filled a gourd
with the milk and set it near the door.

6
00:00:29,650 --> 00:00:34,194
After playing with my friends that
morning, I ran home. As I entered the

7
00:00:34,234 --> 00:00:39,231
house, I accidentally hit the milk gourd
near the door with my foot and knocked

8
00:00:39,271 --> 00:00:39,747
it over.

9
00:00:40,150 --> 00:00:45,146
Every drop spilled onto the ground.
Startled, I immediately looked at my

10
00:00:45,186 --> 00:00:45,643
mother.

11
00:00:46,150 --> 00:00:51,769
My mother always has something she says
when startled. That day, as usual, she

12
00:00:51,809 --> 00:00:53,900
shouted, “Jesus of Nazareth!”

13
00:00:54,150 --> 00:00:59,530
After making sure I was not hurt, she
picked up a stick and came toward me.

14
00:00:59,570 --> 00:01:05,389
When I realized where things were going,
I got up and ran for it. I had never run

15
00:01:05,429 --> 00:01:10,003
like I did that day. Even our cows stood
watching the spectacle.

16
00:01:10,650 --> 00:01:15,513
The milk spilled, and I went the day
without drinking the milk I had run for.

17
00:01:15,553 --> 00:01:20,416
My mother said her usual proverb about
haste leading to spills and picking up

18
00:01:20,456 --> 00:01:25,189
the pieces. It remains a memory that
makes us laugh even today. Mom, I love

19
00:01:25,229 --> 00:01:25,964
you so much!
